.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt UUX 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uux
.Nd queue a command for a configured uucp peer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl bcCjnz
.Op Fl a Ar user
.Op Fl g Ar grade
.Op Fl x Ar debug
.Ar command-string
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility parses a
.Ql system!command
string and queues it under
.Pa /var/spool/uucp .
No remote command is executed in this image.
.Pp
Words may be single- or double-quoted; a backslash quotes the next character.
The supported redirections are
.Ql < Ar file
for a local input file,
.Ql < Fl
for the serial-console standard input, and
.Ql >
or
.Ql >>
followed by an output name.
Pipes, command lists, globbing and shell expansion are not interpreted.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b
Accept the break compatibility flag.
.It Fl c
Accept the spool-copy compatibility flag. The queue always embeds the input payload.
.It Fl C
Same as
.Fl c .
.It Fl j
Print the queued job id.
.It Fl n
Never mail completion.
.It Fl z
Mail on success (recorded flag; no mail transport exists).
.It Fl a Ar user
Set the requesting user name.
.It Fl g Ar grade
Set the one-byte job grade (default
.Ql n ) .
.It Fl x Ar debug
Parse and ignore a debug level.
.El
.Pp
An unknown peer is an error. The peer list and spool root come from
.Pa /etc/uucp/config ;
see
.Xr uucp 1 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/spool/uucp -compact
.It Pa /etc/uucp/config
Peer and spool configuration.
.It Pa /var/spool/uucp/queue
Queued job records.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A missing input, unknown peer or queue error exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uucp 1 ,
.Xr uustat 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements a bounded POSIX uux command-queueing subset. Command execution and the
.Fl p ,
.Fl r
and
.Fl s
forms are not implemented.
